//! Types moved out of `iyakki_agent::settingstools_geminivoice` (F-SPLIT-03, scripted by dist/split/move_types.py); the agent re-exports them.



pub const PROMPT_RULE: &str = "\nGEMINI VOICE ASSISTANT (Settings -> Models, EXPERIMENTAL, off by default): a live voice session with Google Gemini: while it is open the microphone is sent to Google and a red sign shows; Gemini's answer text is read aloud by the local voice. gemini_voice_status says whether it is on, whether a key is stored (never the key), whether the person said yes to sending the microphone, the start key, the limits and today's microphone time. gemini_voice_set (enabled, key, model, max_session_secs, idle_secs, day_cap_secs, spoken_cap_chars, wake_handoff, voice_out, language) asks the person every time. In a voice session the live model gets the same tools as the chat, through the same approvals: a tool that asks shows its card on the screen and a spoken yes never approves it. In the status the delay from the end of the person's speech to the first sound of the answer is logged. gemini_voice_stop closes an open session at once and needs no approval. You cannot type the key and you cannot give the consent: the person answers the consent card on the Settings page. Never start this for private talk on the free tier, where Google may use what is sent to improve its products (according to Google's published terms).";
